From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 13:27:18 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] feat(network): hold synchronization on metered connections

Motivation: synchronization downloads and uploads whole files at any time.
On a connection the desktop marks as metered (a phone hotspot, a capped
plan) that spends the person's data without their choice.

Changes: while GLib's network monitor reports the connection as metered,
saved scopes are not started at launch and running ones are stopped through
stop_synchronization; when the connection is no longer metered they are
started again with the saved configuration. The person is told once by a
notification, by a banner in the window (with a button to Preferences) and
by the tray's tooltip. Preferences > Background gains "Synchronize on
Metered Connections" (off by default); turning it on applies at once.
Nothing is deleted and no configuration changes.

Validation: cargo fmt --check, cargo clippy -D warnings, the preferences
round-trip test; in a Plasma session with NetworkManager's Metered property
switched on and off, the workers stop and start again, the banner, the tray
and the notification say so, and the stand-in sees no Drive request while
the connection is metered.

Limitations: GLib reads the metered state from NetworkManager (or the
network portal in a sandbox); without either it reports not metered.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (claude-opus-5-5)
Origin: vendor, Sparky Stereo OS (branch order299 of the edition's DriveSync fork)
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-11-27
